 ],
 "literal": "Of the expanse of shining water where leaping sharks bustle, / with fragrant blossoms of ñāḻal, the puṉṉai spreads, / the lord of the shore who appears like the arena where the Veri ritual is performed, / whether he does not intend or whether he intends, other than him, / to one who does not know, shall I speak? I, / on that day when he embraced these emaciated, bamboo-like, beautiful, soft shoulders, / made an unfailing oath. / The thief, the duty-bound one, and the one who adorns is himself indeed.",
 "translation": "On the expanse of shining waters where leaping sharks bustle, the mastwood tree scatters its blossoms along with the fragrant ñāḻal, making the shore look like the arena where the Veri ritual is performed. Whether the lord of that shore intends to marry me or not, shall I speak of this to anyone else who does not understand? On that day when he embraced these now-wasted, beautiful, soft shoulders, he made an unfailing oath. He is the thief who stole my heart, he is the one bound by duty to marry me, and he is the one who must adorn me.",
 "modern": "பாய்ந்து செல்லும் சுறா மீன்கள் நிறைந்த, விளங்குகின்ற நீர்ப்பரப்பில், நறிய மலர்களைக் கொண்ட ஞாழல் மரத்தோடு புன்னை மரத்தின் மலர்களும் உதிர்ந்து பரவிக் கிடக்கின்றன. அது வெறியாடும் களம் போலத் தோன்றும் கடற்கரைத் துறைக்குத் தலைவன் அவன். அவன் என்னை மணக்க நினைத்தாலும், நினைக்காவிட்டாலும், என் நிலையை அறியாத பிறரிடம் நான் இதைப் பற்றிப் பேசுவேனோ? மெலிந்துபோன, மூங்கில் போன்ற அழகிய என் மெல்லிய தோள்களை அவன் தழுவிய அந்த நாளில், அவன் தவறாத சூளுரை உரைத்தான். என் நெஞ்சைக் கவர்ந்த கள்வனும் அவனே; என்னை மணக்க வேண்டிய கடமை உடையவனும் அவனே; எனக்கு அணிகலன்கள் சூட்டி அழகு செய்ய வேண்டியவனும் அவனே ஆவான்.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her confidante about the hero's delay in marrying her. She describes his coastal land, where the fallen yellow flowers of the ñāḻal and white flowers of the puṉṉai trees scatter on the sand, making the shore look like a ritual ground prepared for the Veri dance. This vivid image reflects her inner turmoil, as her family is considering performing a Veri ritual to cure her wasting sickness, not knowing it is caused by her love. She declares that whether the hero intends to marry her soon or not, she cannot reveal her secret love to anyone who does not understand. She recalls the solemn, unfailing oath he made when he first embraced her beautiful, soft shoulders. Ultimately, she asserts that he is the thief who stole her heart, the debtor bound by duty to marry her, and the protector who must restore her beauty.",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
 "generated": "2026-11-26"
}